# Command: MW (Set frame)
# Radio: Kenwood TS-480HX / TS-480SAT
# Title (cover, verbatim): "PC CONTROL COMMAND REFERENCE FOR THE TS-480HX/ SAT
#   TRANSCEIVER"
# Printed revision: NONE printed; cover carries "KENWOOD CORPORATION",
#   "(c) 2003/11/28" and the printing code line "09 08 07 06 05 04 03 02 01 00".
# Source page: printed folio "14"  ==  PDF page 15 of 26
# Charts used: the "Set" chart of the MW block.  The block ALSO prints a "Read" row
#   and an "Answer" row, each with its ruler 1..10 drawn and every one of its ten
#   cells EMPTY - see FINDING F3.
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTHS (two independent counts of the printed numbered ruler):
#   MW Set    = 50 positions  (five ruler rows: 1-10, 11-20, 21-30, 31-40, 41-50)
#   MW Read   = 0 positions filled (ruler printed 1..10, every cell empty)
#   MW Answer = 0 positions filled (ruler printed 1..10, every cell empty)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SET CHART, position by position:
#   1  M          2  W
#   3  P1
#   4  P2         5-6  P3
#   7-17  P4      (11 positions)
#   18  P5
#   19  P6
#   20  P7
#   21-22  P8
#   23-24  P9
#   25-27  P10
#   28  P11
#   29  P12
#   30-38  P13   (9 positions)
#   39-40  P14
#   41  P15
#   42-49  P16   (8 positions)
#   50  ;
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEGEND, VERBATIM (the complete right-hand column, headed "Parameters:"; block
# description reads "Store the data to the Memory channel."):
#
#   P1
#     0: RX frequency, 1: TX frequency
#   P2
#     Always 0 for the TS-480.
#   P3
#     00 ~ 99: Memory channel number
#   P4
#     Frequency in Hz (11-digit).
#   P5
#     Mode.  Refer to the MD command.
#   P6
#     Lockout status.  0: Lockout OFF, 1: Lockout ON
#   P7
#     0: OFF, 1: TONE, 2: CTCSS
#   P8
#     Tone Number.  Refero to the TN command.
#   P9
#     CTCSS tone number.  Refer to the CN command.
#   P10
#     Always 000 for the TS-480.
#   P11
#     Always 0 for the TS-480.
#   P12
#     Always 0 for the TS-480.
#   P13
#     Always 000000000 for the TS-480.
#   P14
#     Step size.  Refer to the ST command.
#   P15
#     Always 0 for the TS-480.
#   P16
#     Memory name.  A maximum of 8 characters.
#
#   Memory channel 90 ~ 99:
#   P1=0 (start frequency), P1=1 (end frequency)
#
#   (P8 is transcribed exactly as printed: "Refero".  MR's P8 in the SAME book reads
#    "Tone Number.  Refer to page 35." - see FINDINGS F4 and F6.)
#
# WHAT THE BOOK SAYS ABOUT OMITTING THE NAME OR SENDING A SHORTER FRAME, AND WHAT
# HAPPENS TO THE CHANNEL THEN:
#   NOTHING.  The MW block of this book prints no statement at all about omitting
#   P16, about a shorter frame, or about erasing a channel.  (Compare the TS-590
#   book, whose MW block does carry such a note.)  The only nearby general statement
#   in the whole document is the folio-2 note, VERBATIM:
#     "Note:  If a particular parameter is not applicable to this transceiver, the
#      parameter digits should be filled using any character except the ASCII control
#      codes (00 to 1Fh) and the terminator (;)."
#   No erase vector is emitted here, because no shorter-frame shape is printed.
#
# EVERY POSITION THE CHART PRINTS AS FIXED / "Always" (by position number):
#   position  4         (P2)   -- "Always 0 for the TS-480."
#   positions 25,26,27  (P10)  -- "Always 000 for the TS-480."
#   position  28        (P11)  -- "Always 0 for the TS-480."
#   position  29        (P12)  -- "Always 0 for the TS-480."
#   positions 30..38    (P13)  -- "Always 000000000 for the TS-480."
#   position  41        (P15)  -- "Always 0 for the TS-480."
#   (No "not used" note appears in the MW block.)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTES WHOSE VALUE THE MANUAL DOES NOT DETERMINE  -> INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   [B1] positions 7..17 (P4) - the frequency VALUE in each vector is ASSUMED; only
#        the 11-digit Hz format is documented.
#   [B2] positions 42..49 (P16) when the name is shorter than 8.  The book says
#        NOTHING about padding.  Not exercised below (both names are exactly 8).
#   [B3] positions 21..22 (P8) and 23..24 (P9) when the tone system is OFF -
#        ASSUMED "00"; no don't-care value is printed.
#   [B4] positions 39..40 (P14) VALUES - the width 2 follows the chart and the ST
#        legend, but the value in each vector is ASSUMED.
#   [B5] The channel numbers, mode digits and name strings are ASSUMED illustrative
#        values; only their field widths and legends are documented.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED for every vector in this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VECTORS  (name <TAB> frame bytes verbatim, terminator included)
#
# Mirrors mr480_answer_ch03_rx_name8: RX frequency, tone OFF, 8-character name
mw480_set_ch03_rx_name8	MW000300014250000200000000000000000000000DXCLUSTR;
# Mirrors mr480_answer_ch12_tx_tone_on: TX frequency, TONE on (P8=08), 10 kHz step
mw480_set_ch12_tx_tone_on	MW101200051500000401080000000000000000020REPEATER;
